//! fail
//! error-any: invalid UTF-8 sequence at byte 0xE9
//! error-any: char literal holds exactly one character
// A lone CR is whitespace or a byte of a comment, and it ends no line (D2.1). After a lexical
// error the resync drops the rest of the line, the bytes after a lone CR included, so each of
// lines 10 and 11 gives 1 error (D14.2). The harness reads a lone CR as a line end, so the
// error-any lines and the golden hold the errors with their lines and columns.
fn main() i32 {
    println("a");
    // é// ÿ
    'ab''cd';
    return 0;
}
